<problem>
<!-- <title>discrete equilibria 2</title> -->

<setup>

<selectFromSequence name="r1" from="1" to=" 7" />
<selectFromSequence name="b" from="1" to=" 20" />
<selectFromSequence name="r2" from="8" to=" 15" />
<select name="x"> x y z u v w p X Y Z </select>

<math name="answer" unordered="true">$r1 ,-$r1 ,$r2 ,-$r2 </math>
<math name="R1" simplify="full">$r1 **2</math>
<math name="R2" simplify="full">$r2 **2</math>

</setup>


<p>Find all equilibria to the discrete dynamical system below.  If there are multiple equilibria, separate your answers by commas.  
<md>
  <mrow>$x _{n+1} - $x _n\amp = ( $x _n^2 - $R1  )( $x _n^2 - $R2  )</mrow>
  <mrow>$x _0\amp = $b</mrow>
</md>
</p>

<p><m>E =</m> 
<answer>
<award matchPartial="true" unorderedCompare="true">$answer </award>
</answer>
</p>


<solution>
<p>To find the equilibria, we set <m>$x _{n+1} = E</m> and <m>$x _n = E</m> in the evolution rule, obtaining
<md>
  <mrow>E-E\amp =  ( E^2 - $R1  )( E^2- $R2  )</mrow>
  <mrow>0\amp = ( E^2 - $R1  )( E^2 - $R2  )</mrow>
</md>
Therefore, either <m>E^2 = $R1 </m> or <m>E^2 = $R2 </m>.  The equilibria are <m>E=$r1 </m>, <m>E=-$r1 </m>, <m>E=$r2 </m>, and <m>E=-$r2 </m>.</p>


</solution>


</problem>